WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:05.310
There's no Peter Parker or Miles Morales in
the trailer for "Madame Web," but plenty of

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.020
other Spider-People appear.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:11.096
Who are they, and how close are their costumes
to their comics counterparts?

00:00:11.096 --> 00:00:15.330
Fans of Sony's Spider-Man universe have had
to do some waiting this year, as the release

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:21.054
date for "Kraven the Hunter" was pushed back
from October 2023 to August 2024.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:25.530
But they at least got the trailer for "Madame
Web," yet another adaptation of a classic

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:27.362
"Spider-Man" character from the studio.

00:00:27.362 --> 00:00:32.250
The 2024 feature will star Dakota Johnson
as the clairvoyant title character.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:36.340
It seems as though she will find herself protecting
a new generation of Spider-heroes in three

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:41.680
young women: Julia Carpenter played by Sydney
Sweeney, Mattie Franklin played by Celeste

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:45.333
O'Connor, and Anya Corazon played by Isabella
Merced.

00:00:45.333 --> 00:00:47.414
"I can see the future.

00:00:47.414 --> 00:00:48.530
Oh!

00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:49.530
What the hell?"

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.594
"She didn't see that coming."

00:00:51.122 --> 00:00:52.301
"That's not how it works."

00:00:52.301 --> 00:00:56.630
Perhaps due to their connection to one another
and the wider web of Spider-people, these

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:01.850
soon-to-be Spider-Women must survive being
hunted by Ezekiel Sims, a deadly operator

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.914
with as-of-yet unknown motivations-- played
by Tahir Rahim.

00:01:05.914 --> 00:01:10.060
Ezekiel Sims is the odd-spider-out in the
trailer — and that's not just because he's

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:11.650
trying to kill everyone else.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.670
The character wears a chilling black-and-red
suit that is a far cry from the character's

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:16.830
comics attire.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:21.350
In the comics, Sims has powers almost identical
to those of Peter Parker, but received them

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:24.040
long before as part of an ancient ritual.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:28.460
Instead of becoming a superhero, he became
an immensely powerful businessman who would

00:01:28.460 --> 00:01:30.159
use his powers sparingly.

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:34.569
So the comics version of Ezekiel doesn't really
have a costume in the traditional sense.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:39.500
In one alternate universe, Sims steals a costume
from a variant of Spider-Man that was killed

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:44.250
by Morlun, one of the Inheritors, who is basically
an energy vampire.

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:48.689
Ezekiel's typical comics apparel doesn't appear
to have influenced his "Madame Web" look,

00:01:48.689 --> 00:01:53.850
probably at least in part due to a casually
dressed villain cutting in on action figure sales.

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.260
"Euphoria" star Sydney Sweeney will make her
superhero debut with "Madame Web," playing

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.649
the seemingly bookish Julia Carpenter.

00:02:00.649 --> 00:02:05.899
In the comics, she has adopted the monikers
Spider-Woman, Arachne, and even Madame Web,

00:02:05.899 --> 00:02:07.810
all after someone else had those names.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:11.820
It appears as though Sweeney will be sporting
the original black-and-white bodysuit Carpenter

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:16.690
wore when she first debuted in the first "Secret
Wars" series in 1984.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:21.040
The design of this costume — especially
its sprawling, white insignia — will likely

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.800
remind fans of another character: Venom.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:29.449
Unlike Peter Parker's symbiote suit that became
Venom, there's nothing alien about Carpenter's outfit.

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:33.900
Carpenter's suit actually debuted the issue
before Parker's did, and it's stated that

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.069
the now-iconic white symbiote spider symbol
was subconsciously inspired by her design.

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:43.290
It would be a clever twist if Sony adapted
this story beat, and allowed Tom Hardy's Eddie

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:47.494
Brock to finally adopt the emblem after seeing
Sweeney's Carpenter in action.

00:02:47.494 --> 00:02:49.160
"Why would I do that?"

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:55.492
Anya Corazon was first introduced in a 2004
issue of "Amazing Fantasy" as the superhero Araña.

00:02:55.492 --> 00:03:00.090
She has two main comics costume styles, one
of which includes the large, bug-eyed goggles

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.080
seen for a brief moment in the trailer.

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:07.870
Her first costume is a relatively casual/tactical
outfit that consists of a vest, tank top,

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:11.730
and jeans, all of which fit a red, black,
and yellow color motif.

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:16.069
After meeting Julia Carpenter, Corazon is
given a black bodysuit with white accents

00:03:16.069 --> 00:03:17.840
very similar to her new friend's.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:22.310
Under the new alias "Spider-Girl," Corazon
wears this black-and-white suit through several

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:27.049
minor alterations until it is destroyed by
the supervillain Vermin, at which point she

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:29.594
returns to something closer to her original
look.

00:03:29.594 --> 00:03:33.810
Based on the very brief look at Corazon's
costume in the "Madame Web" trailer, it appears

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:37.930
as though she'll be wearing something closer
to her second costume, but with the goggles

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:39.470
from the first.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:43.400
Unlike her friends' black costumes, Mattie
Franklin wears the traditional blue-and-red

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:45.010
colors of Peter Parker's Spider-Man.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:49.400
That may be a nod to her uniquely close comics
connection to the original Web-Slinger.

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:54.050
After getting super powers in the mystical
"Gathering of Five" ceremony organized by

00:03:54.050 --> 00:03:59.599
Norman Osborn, Mattie briefly took over for
Peter as Spider-Man while he was temporarily retired.

00:03:59.599 --> 00:04:03.471
After Peter put the webs back on, she became
the third Spider-Woman.

00:04:03.471 --> 00:04:08.129
Her infatuation with Peter created some bizarre
friction between them, though we don't expect

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:10.140
that to play into her role in "Madame Web."

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:13.810
That's because lots of signs point to "Madame
Web" being a prequel of sorts.

00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:19.180
A popular theory online speculates, and his
IMDb credits indicate, that Adam Scott's suspiciously

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:23.930
unnamed character is actually a young Ben
Parker — Peter's uncle, who dies in most

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.817
versions of his origin story.

00:04:25.817 --> 00:04:30.600
That'd mean "Madame Web" takes place well
before any other "Spider-Man" story, and Franklin

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.460
couldn't have any connection to the most famous
wallcrawler around.

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:39.337
Fans will have to wait and see when "Madame
Web" debuts on February 14, 2024.

